# SoapBoxx

Follow as source of truth (repo root): `SOAPBOXX_V1_7DAY_EXECUTION.md` (build ONLY current day; no redesign), `SOAPBOXX_EXECUTION_PLAN_V1.md`, `SOAPBOXX_MASTER_PLAN_FOUNDATION.md`, `PRODUCT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `WORKFLOW.md`, `RULES.md`, `BRANCHES.md`. V1 stack target: FastAPI+Postgres+Redis+Celery per 7-day plan. No coach/scoring/ranking. Missing scope → V1 vs V2, not new architecture.

## Core loop

Record → Transcribe → Improve. Changes must improve recording, transcription, feedback, or workflow clarity.

## Branches

- Active development: **`production`** only
- **`demo`**: fast-forward from `production` before demo packages; no feature commits on demo branch alone
- Do not use `main`, `Local`, or `demo/soapboxx-barebones` for new work

## Code paths

- Desktop UI: `SoapBoxxCore` → `transcriber` → `FeedbackEngine` (Reverb tab)
- Do not extend `soapboxx_v3_workflow` / `blueprint_v1` / `atomic_pipeline` for UI unless explicitly requested
- Do not add new AI client layers; consolidate through `backend/llm_service.py` when touching LLM code

## Ignore (not source)

`releases/**`, `SoapBoxx-Distribution*/**`, `SoapBoxx-Demo-Distribution/**`, `reports/**`

## Refactors

No drive-by refactors. No duplicate logic across modules. If a request conflicts with these rules, ask before proceeding.
